 doesn't matter that much to me i have no  real pressing need to engage in small  talk chit chat  um but i am motivated by these  interesting content items and so i kind  of liken it to  you know i scoop up a lot of stuff and i  keep on scooping up a lot of stuff in  this huge basket and it's all swimming  around in there  maybe interacting you know maybe it's  fish and they're kind of interacting in  some way and  and i scoop up more and more all in this  big in this big  basket  and eventually more and more of that  stays  whereas if i go and grab  stuff with a little basket and throw it  onto the shore  i find i tend to lose a lot of it it  could be reviewing  you know  endings of verbs reviewing certain  patterns of speech i mean you have to do  some of it you have to do some of it all  along you have to do some of it at the  very beginning and you have to do it  sort of regularly throughout but all of  i find all of those kinds of reviews of  structure and of grammatical rules and  case endings  uh stays with you for a very short time  it's like you picked it up in a small  fishnet and you put it on the shore and  you looked at it and pretty soon it kind  of all went away a little bit remains  but mostly it kind of goes away whereas  the stuff that we pick up in this big  basket and that's what i do when i'm  listening to difficult stuff and reading  difficult stuff and accumulating all  these words very few of them do i have  time to review and flash cards most of  the time i'm just meeting them again  highlighted in yellow at link in  in you know the next lesson and stuff  and it's just it's always there and  and eventually it starts to settle  and  again you go back to the rules and that  but eventually as it settles you've got  more and more of a of sort of a  background  of experience  against which you can then apply these  little rules that you're constantly  learning and forgetting learning and  forgetting learning and forgetting  and so i guess what i'